// Banco de perguntas originais, escritas para o exame de maio 2026 (7 secções).
// s = secção (1..7), m = mock (1 ou 2), a = índice da resposta certa (0-based)
// Perguntas em inglês (como no exame); explicações em português.
window.SECTIONS = {
  1: { name: "Databricks Intelligence Platform", w: 6 },
  2: { name: "Data Ingestion and Loading", w: 21 },
  3: { name: "Data Transformation and Modeling", w: 22 },
  4: { name: "Working with Lakeflow Jobs", w: 16 },
  5: { name: "Implementing CI/CD", w: 10 },
  6: { name: "Troubleshooting, Monitoring and Optimization", w: 10 },
  7: { name: "Governance and Security", w: 15 }
};

window.QUESTIONS = [
// ───────────────────────── MOCK 1 ─────────────────────────
// S1
{m:1,s:1,q:"Which statement about the Databricks architecture is correct?",
 o:["The control plane runs in the customer's cloud account when classic compute is used",
    "The control plane is always hosted in the Databricks account; classic compute runs in the customer's cloud account",
    "Serverless compute runs in the customer's cloud account",
    "Both planes always run in the customer's cloud account"],
 a:1, e:"O control plane (UI, gestão de jobs, notebooks) está sempre na conta Databricks. O compute plane clássico corre na tua conta cloud; o serverless corre na conta Databricks."},
{m:1,s:1,q:"A team runs a nightly Python ETL in production and wants the lowest cost compute option. Which should they AVOID?",
 o:["Serverless jobs compute","Job compute (classic)","All-purpose compute","A job cluster shared across tasks with job_cluster_key"],
 a:2, e:"All-purpose compute é para desenvolvimento interativo e é o mais caro. Jobs em produção correm em job compute ou serverless jobs."},
{m:1,s:1,q:"An older study guide mentions 'Delta Live Tables (DLT)'. What is the current name of this product?",
 o:["Lakeflow Connect","Lakeflow Jobs","Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines","Declarative Automation Bundles"],
 a:2, e:"DLT → Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines. Workflows → Lakeflow Jobs. Asset Bundles → Declarative Automation Bundles. Repos → Git folders."},
// S2
{m:1,s:2,q:"Millions of JSON files land continuously in cloud storage and new fields are added over time. Which ingestion method is the best fit?",
 o:["COPY INTO scheduled every minute","Auto Loader (cloudFiles) with schema evolution","CREATE TABLE AS SELECT with read_files","Lakehouse Federation"],
 a:1, e:"Auto Loader escala para milhões de ficheiros, processa incrementalmente e suporta schema evolution. COPY INTO é bom para milhares de ficheiros."},
{m:1,s:2,q:"A data engineer runs the same COPY INTO command twice without new files arriving. What happens on the second run?",
 o:["All files are loaded again, creating duplicates","The command fails because the files were already loaded","No new rows are loaded because already-loaded files are skipped","The target table is overwritten"],
 a:2, e:"COPY INTO é idempotente: guarda quais ficheiros já carregou e ignora-os."},
{m:1,s:2,q:"A source file with errors was already loaded by COPY INTO. A corrected file with the SAME name is uploaded. How do you load it again?",
 o:["Use FORMAT_OPTIONS ('mergeSchema' = 'true')","Use COPY_OPTIONS ('force' = 'true')","Run VACUUM on the target first","Rename the target table"],
 a:1, e:"COPY INTO ignora ficheiros já carregados mesmo que tenham sido modificados. 'force'='true' em COPY_OPTIONS obriga a recarregar."},
{m:1,s:2,q:"An Auto Loader stream uses cloudFiles.schemaEvolutionMode = 'rescue'. A new column appears in the source files. What happens?",
 o:["The stream fails and adds the column on restart","The new column is added to the table schema automatically","The schema is not changed; the new data goes to the _rescued_data column","The new column is silently dropped with no trace"],
 a:2, e:"'rescue' nunca evolui o schema: os dados inesperados ficam em _rescued_data. Quem falha e evolui ao reiniciar é 'addNewColumns'."},
{m:1,s:2,q:"Auto Loader is configured WITHOUT a schema and with default settings. A new column appears. What is the behavior?",
 o:["The stream fails with an UnknownFieldException; after restart the new column is included",
    "The column is written to _rescued_data and the stream continues",
    "The stream ignores the column forever",
    "The stream fails and the column is never added"],
 a:0, e:"Sem schema, o modo por defeito é addNewColumns: o stream falha, atualiza o schema no schemaLocation e ao reiniciar inclui a coluna."},
{m:1,s:2,q:"A company needs to ingest data from Salesforce into Delta tables without writing or maintaining API code. What should they use?",
 o:["Auto Loader","A notebook with the requests library","Lakeflow Connect managed connector","COPY INTO"],
 a:2, e:"Para SaaS e bases de dados suportadas (Salesforce, Workday, SQL Server…) o caminho é Lakeflow Connect (managed connectors)."},
{m:1,s:2,q:"Analysts need to run occasional queries against an operational PostgreSQL database without copying the data into Databricks. What is the best option?",
 o:["Lakehouse Federation","Auto Loader","Lakeflow Connect managed connector","Delta Sharing"],
 a:0, e:"Lakehouse Federation permite consultar fontes externas sem copiar os dados. 'Sem copiar' é a palavra-chave."},
{m:1,s:2,q:"Which trigger makes a Structured Streaming / Auto Loader query process all data currently available and then stop?",
 o:["trigger(processingTime='0 seconds')","trigger(continuous='1 second')","trigger(availableNow=True)","No trigger (default)"],
 a:2, e:"availableNow=True processa tudo o que está disponível (em vários micro-batches) e pára. Ideal para ingestão incremental agendada num job."},
{m:1,s:2,q:"A STRING column 'raw' contains JSON like {\"customer\":{\"address\":{\"city\":\"Lisbon\"}}}. Which SQL expression extracts the city?",
 o:["raw.customer.address.city","raw:customer.address.city","raw->customer->address->city","get_json(raw, 'city')"],
 a:1, e:"Para strings JSON (e VARIANT) usa-se a sintaxe com dois pontos: raw:customer.address.city. A notação só com pontos é para STRUCT."},
// S3
{m:1,s:3,code:"df1 = spark.createDataFrame([(1,'Ana')], ['id','name'])\ndf2 = spark.createDataFrame([('Rui',2)], ['name','id'])\nresult = df1.union(df2)",
 q:"What is the problem with this code?",
 o:["union removes duplicates","union matches columns by position, so names and ids are mixed up; use unionByName","union fails because the DataFrames have different column order","There is no problem"],
 a:1, e:"union em PySpark junta por posição (e não remove duplicados). Com colunas em ordem diferente, usa unionByName."},
{m:1,s:3,q:"Table A has 3 rows and table B has the same 3 rows. How many rows does SELECT * FROM A UNION SELECT * FROM B return?",
 o:["0","3","6","An error"],
 a:1, e:"UNION em SQL remove duplicados (equivale a UNION DISTINCT). UNION ALL devolveria 6. Atenção: df.union() em PySpark mantém duplicados."},
{m:1,s:3,q:"A query uses WHERE discount = NULL and returns no rows, although some rows have NULL in discount. What is the fix?",
 o:["WHERE discount == NULL","WHERE discount IS NULL","WHERE discount = 'NULL'","WHERE isnull = discount"],
 a:1, e:"Qualquer comparação com NULL usando = dá NULL (nunca verdadeiro). Usa IS NULL / isNull(), ou <=> para comparação null-safe."},
{m:1,s:3,q:"You need to keep only the most recent record per customer_id based on updated_at. Which approach guarantees this?",
 o:["df.dropDuplicates(['customer_id'])",
    "df.distinct()",
    "row_number() over a window partitioned by customer_id ordered by updated_at desc, then filter row number = 1",
    "df.groupBy('customer_id').count()"],
 a:2, e:"dropDuplicates fica com uma linha qualquer. Para a mais recente usa row_number() numa janela ordenada (em SQL também QUALIFY)."},
{m:1,s:3,q:"Which join returns customers that have NO matching rows in the orders table, with only the customer columns?",
 o:["left_outer","left_semi","left_anti","cross"],
 a:2, e:"left_anti = linhas da esquerda SEM correspondência. left_semi = linhas da esquerda COM correspondência. Ambas devolvem só colunas da esquerda."},
{m:1,s:3,q:"A column 'tags' is an array; some rows have NULL or empty arrays. You must keep those rows in the output with a NULL tag. Which function?",
 o:["explode","explode_outer","flatten","posexplode"],
 a:1, e:"explode descarta linhas com array NULL ou vazio; explode_outer mantém-nas com NULL."},
{m:1,s:3,q:"A customer dimension must keep the full history of address changes with validity periods. Which approach in a declarative pipeline?",
 o:["AUTO CDC ... STORED AS SCD TYPE 1","AUTO CDC ... STORED AS SCD TYPE 2","A materialized view with INSERT OVERWRITE","A view"],
 a:1, e:"SCD tipo 2 guarda histórico (colunas __START_AT / __END_AT). SCD tipo 1 (o defeito do AUTO CDC) sobrescreve."},
{m:1,s:3,code:"CONSTRAINT valid_amount EXPECT (amount > 0) ON VIOLATION DROP ROW",
 q:"What happens to a row with amount = -5?",
 o:["The pipeline update fails","The row is written and the violation is only logged","The row is dropped and the violation is recorded in metrics","The row is sent to a quarantine table automatically"],
 a:2, e:"DROP ROW descarta a linha (e conta nas métricas). Sem ON VIOLATION só regista (warn) e mantém. FAIL UPDATE pára o flow."},
{m:1,s:3,q:"You need to apply inserts and updates from a daily batch of changes into an existing Delta table, matching on id. Which command?",
 o:["INSERT INTO","INSERT OVERWRITE","MERGE INTO ... WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT","COPY INTO"],
 a:2, e:"MERGE é o comando de upsert (e SCD1). A fonte deve vir deduplicada, senão o MERGE falha por várias linhas coincidirem com a mesma linha alvo."},
{m:1,s:3,q:"In a star schema, which table typically contains quantities and amounts plus foreign keys?",
 o:["Dimension table","Fact table","Bridge view","Bronze table"],
 a:1, e:"Factos = eventos e medidas (quanto? quantos?) + chaves estrangeiras. Dimensões = atributos descritivos (quem, o quê, quando, onde)."},
// S4
{m:1,s:4,q:"A job has a cleanup task that must run after the other tasks, whether they succeed or fail. Which 'Run if' condition?",
 o:["ALL_SUCCESS","ALL_DONE","AT_LEAST_ONE_FAILED","NONE_FAILED"],
 a:1, e:"ALL_DONE corre quando todas as dependências terminam, seja qual for o resultado."},
{m:1,s:4,q:"A 6-task job failed at task 4. Tasks 1–3 succeeded. How can you re-run only what is needed?",
 o:["Run now again","Repair run","Clone the job","Reset the job"],
 a:1, e:"Repair run volta a correr apenas as tasks que falharam e as que dependem delas. Cuidado com tasks que fazem append."},
{m:1,s:4,q:"Task A computes a row count that Task B needs. What is the recommended way to pass the value?",
 o:["Write it to a global temp view","dbutils.jobs.taskValues.set() in A and taskValues.get() in B","Use a widget with the same name","Environment variables on the cluster"],
 a:1, e:"Task values: set na task A, get na task B (ou referência dinâmica {{tasks.A.values.key}})."},
{m:1,s:4,q:"Files from a partner arrive at unpredictable times in a Unity Catalog volume. The job should start shortly after each arrival. Which trigger?",
 o:["Scheduled","Continuous","File arrival","Manual"],
 a:2, e:"File arrival trigger monitoriza um volume ou external location e dispara o job quando chegam ficheiros novos."},
{m:1,s:4,q:"A job parameter and a task parameter have the same key 'env'. Which value does the task receive?",
 o:["The task parameter","The job parameter","Neither – the job fails","A random one"],
 a:1, e:"Os parâmetros do job sobrepõem-se aos da task com a mesma chave."},
{m:1,s:4,q:"A task occasionally fails because of a transient network error. What configuration addresses this with the least effort?",
 o:["Increase the cluster size","Set a retry policy on the task (max retries, interval)","Change the trigger to Continuous","Add a second identical task"],
 a:1, e:"Retries são configurados por task (max_retries por defeito é 0). Também existe retry_on_timeout."},
{m:1,s:4,q:"Which statement about the Continuous trigger is correct?",
 o:["It runs on a Quartz cron schedule","It keeps one run always active and starts a new run when the previous one ends","It requires a file arrival location","It supports task-level retries the same way as scheduled jobs"],
 a:1, e:"Continuous mantém sempre um run ativo; quando termina, arranca outro. Não usa retries como os jobs agendados."},
// S5
{m:1,s:5,q:"Which command checks a bundle's configuration for errors and shows the resolved configuration, without deploying anything?",
 o:["databricks bundle init","databricks bundle validate","databricks bundle run","databricks bundle destroy"],
 a:1, e:"Fluxo: init → validate → deploy → run. validate não altera nada no workspace."},
{m:1,s:5,q:"How do you deploy a bundle to the 'prod' target?",
 o:["databricks bundle deploy --env prod","databricks bundle deploy -t prod","databricks deploy prod","databricks bundle run prod"],
 a:1, e:"-t / --target escolhe o target definido em databricks.yml. Sem -t usa o target com default: true."},
{m:1,s:5,q:"The same job must write to dev_catalog in dev and prod_catalog in prod. What is the recommended bundle approach?",
 o:["Two separate bundles","A custom variable with a default, overridden in targets.<name>.variables","Hard-code the catalog and edit it before each deploy","Use a widget in the notebook"],
 a:1, e:"Declara a variável em variables (com default) e faz override por target. Referencia com ${var.catalog}."},
{m:1,s:5,q:"How should a CI/CD pipeline (e.g., GitHub Actions) authenticate to deploy bundles to production?",
 o:["With the lead engineer's personal access token","As a service principal using OAuth (M2M or OIDC federation)","With username and password in the YAML","Anonymous access"],
 a:1, e:"Em CI usa-se um service principal com OAuth, nunca um PAT pessoal. Segredos nunca ficam no YAML."},
{m:1,s:5,q:"A developer finished work in a Databricks Git folder and wants it reviewed and merged into main. Where is the pull request created?",
 o:["In the Git folder UI in Databricks","In the Git provider (e.g., GitHub, Azure DevOps)","With databricks bundle deploy","In Catalog Explorer"],
 a:1, e:"Nos Git folders fazes branch, commit, push, pull, merge e rebase; o pull request é feito no fornecedor Git."},
// S6
{m:1,s:6,q:"In the Spark UI, one task of a stage takes 20 minutes while the median task takes 30 seconds. What is the most likely cause?",
 o:["Too many workers","Data skew","Photon is disabled","The table has too few versions"],
 a:1, e:"Uma task muito mais lenta que as outras (max >> mediana) indica skew. Mais workers não resolve; AQE skew join ou salting sim."},
{m:1,s:6,q:"A notebook calls df.collect() on a 500 GB DataFrame and fails with an out-of-memory error on the driver. What fixes it?",
 o:["Add more workers","Avoid bringing the data to the driver (write to a table, aggregate, or use limit)","Increase spark.sql.shuffle.partitions","Enable Photon"],
 a:1, e:"collect() e toPandas() trazem tudo para o driver. Mais workers não ajuda um OOM no driver."},
{m:1,s:6,q:"A join between a 2 TB fact table and a 5 MB lookup table shows a huge shuffle. What is the best optimization?",
 o:["Broadcast the small table","Repartition the large table to 10,000 partitions","Use a cross join","Cache the large table"],
 a:0, e:"Broadcast da tabela pequena evita o shuffle da grande (broadcast(df) ou /*+ BROADCAST(t) */)."},
{m:1,s:6,q:"A Delta table receives frequent small appends and reads are getting slow because of many small files. Which command helps?",
 o:["VACUUM","OPTIMIZE","DESCRIBE HISTORY","RESTORE"],
 a:1, e:"OPTIMIZE compacta ficheiros pequenos. VACUUM só apaga ficheiros já não referenciados (e corta time travel)."},
// S7
{m:1,s:7,q:"A group must be able to read table main.sales.orders. Which privileges are required?",
 o:["SELECT on the table only","USE CATALOG on main, USE SCHEMA on main.sales, and SELECT on the table","READ FILES on the table","ALL PRIVILEGES on the metastore"],
 a:1, e:"Para ler é preciso USE CATALOG + USE SCHEMA + SELECT. Sem os USE, o SELECT sozinho não chega."},
{m:1,s:7,q:"What happens when you run DROP TABLE on an EXTERNAL table in Unity Catalog?",
 o:["Metadata and data files are deleted","Only the metadata is removed; the data files remain in the external location","Nothing; external tables cannot be dropped","The table becomes managed"],
 a:1, e:"External: DROP apaga só metadados. Managed: apaga os dados (UNDROP possível durante 7 dias)."},
{m:1,s:7,q:"A user got SELECT through a grant on the schema. An admin runs REVOKE SELECT ON TABLE t FROM user. What is the result?",
 o:["The user loses access to t","The command fails","The user still has access to t via the schema-level grant","The user loses access to the entire schema"],
 a:2, e:"REVOKE na tabela não tira acesso herdado (e não dá erro). Revoga ao nível onde foi concedido."},
{m:1,s:7,q:"An admin wants to explicitly block one user from a table using DENY in Unity Catalog. What should they know?",
 o:["DENY overrides any GRANT","DENY does not exist in Unity Catalog; access not granted is denied","DENY only works on views","DENY must be combined with REVOKE"],
 a:1, e:"DENY só existe no hive_metastore com table ACLs legacy. No UC, o que não é concedido está negado."},
{m:1,s:7,q:"Only members of the 'hr_admins' group should see the full salary column; everyone else should see NULL. What is the best solution?",
 o:["Create a copy of the table without the column","A column mask function using is_account_group_member('hr_admins')","A row filter","Revoke SELECT from everyone"],
 a:1, e:"Column mask: ALTER TABLE t ALTER COLUMN salary SET MASK fn, onde fn usa is_account_group_member."},
{m:1,s:7,q:"Regional managers should only see rows where region matches their region. What should be used?",
 o:["Column mask","Row filter","Dynamic view with SELECT *","OPTIMIZE ZORDER BY region"],
 a:1, e:"Row filter (ALTER TABLE t SET ROW FILTER fn ON (region)) filtra linhas com base em quem consulta."},
{m:1,s:7,q:"A group needs to read files stored in a Unity Catalog volume. Which privilege is required (besides USE CATALOG / USE SCHEMA)?",
 o:["SELECT","READ VOLUME","READ FILES","BROWSE"],
 a:1, e:"Volumes usam READ VOLUME / WRITE VOLUME. READ FILES é para external locations."},

// ───────────────────────── MOCK 2 ─────────────────────────
// S1
{m:2,s:1,q:"How many Unity Catalog metastores are typically created per cloud region, and how do they relate to workspaces?",
 o:["One per workspace","One per region, attached to multiple workspaces in that region","One per catalog","One global metastore for all regions"],
 a:1, e:"1 metastore UC por região, ligado a vários workspaces; os grants valem em todos."},
{m:2,s:1,q:"A workload uses RDD APIs and R. Which compute should be used?",
 o:["Serverless jobs","Serverless SQL warehouse","Classic job compute with dedicated access mode","Any serverless option"],
 a:2, e:"Serverless não suporta R, RDD nem Spark UI. Precisa de compute clássico (dedicated para R/RDD)."},
{m:2,s:1,q:"What gives Delta Lake its ACID guarantees on top of object storage?",
 o:["The Hive metastore","The _delta_log transaction log","Photon","Parquet statistics only"],
 a:1, e:"Delta = Parquet + _delta_log (log de transações JSON). Daí vêm ACID, time travel, schema enforcement e concorrência otimista."},
// S2
{m:2,s:2,q:"What is the purpose of cloudFiles.schemaLocation in Auto Loader?",
 o:["Where the output table is stored","Where Auto Loader stores the inferred schema and its evolution over time","Where bad records are written","Where checkpoint offsets for Kafka are stored"],
 a:1, e:"schemaLocation guarda o schema inferido e as suas versões. É obrigatório quando se usa inferência de schema."},
{m:2,s:2,q:"COPY INTO must accept new columns that appear in the source files. Which option?",
 o:["COPY_OPTIONS ('mergeSchema' = 'true')","COPY_OPTIONS ('force' = 'true')","FORMAT_OPTIONS ('header' = 'true')","cloudFiles.schemaEvolutionMode = 'addNewColumns'"],
 a:0, e:"mergeSchema em COPY_OPTIONS permite evoluir o schema da tabela. force serve para recarregar ficheiros."},
{m:2,s:2,q:"By default, how does Auto Loader infer column types for JSON and CSV files?",
 o:["Exactly as the data suggests (int, double, date…)","All columns as STRING unless cloudFiles.inferColumnTypes is true","All columns as VARIANT","It requires a schema and cannot infer"],
 a:1, e:"Para JSON/CSV as colunas são inferidas como string, salvo cloudFiles.inferColumnTypes = true."},
{m:2,s:2,q:"Which is the default file detection mode of Auto Loader?",
 o:["File notification","Directory listing","Kafka offsets","Table update"],
 a:1, e:"Por defeito usa directory listing. File notification usa serviços de notificação da cloud (útil para volumes enormes)."},
{m:2,s:2,q:"You must record the source file path of every ingested row. Which column can you select during ingestion?",
 o:["input_file_name only (not supported in UC)","_metadata.file_path","_rescued_data","__START_AT"],
 a:1, e:"A coluna oculta _metadata tem file_path, file_name, file_modification_time, etc. Seleciona-a explicitamente."},
{m:2,s:2,q:"Events arrive in an Apache Kafka topic and must be ingested with low latency. Which approach?",
 o:["COPY INTO","Structured Streaming (or a streaming table) reading from Kafka","Lakehouse Federation","Manual upload"],
 a:1, e:"Kafka/Kinesis → Structured Streaming ou streaming table."},
{m:2,s:2,q:"An analyst wants a SQL-only, idempotent, scheduled load of a few thousand CSV files into an existing Delta table. Which is most appropriate?",
 o:["COPY INTO","Auto Loader with file notification","A Python foreach loop","Lakeflow Connect"],
 a:0, e:"Milhares de ficheiros, SQL, idempotente → COPY INTO."},
{m:2,s:2,q:"Which SQL function reads files directly from a path and can be used in a streaming table definition?",
 o:["read_files","from_json","parse_json","schema_of_json"],
 a:0, e:"read_files lê ficheiros a partir de um caminho; com STREAM read_files numa streaming table usa Auto Loader por baixo."},
{m:2,s:2,q:"Which approach is recommended to store semi-structured JSON whose structure changes frequently?",
 o:["STRING column","VARIANT column (parse_json)","Split into one table per field","BINARY column"],
 a:1, e:"VARIANT (parse_json) é preferível a guardar JSON como string: mais eficiente e flexível."},
// S3
{m:2,s:3,q:"A column 'bonus' has values 100, NULL, 200. What does SELECT count(bonus), count(*) return?",
 o:["3, 3","2, 3","2, 2","3, 2"],
 a:1, e:"count(col), avg e sum ignoram NULL; count(*) conta todas as linhas."},
{m:2,s:3,q:"df has columns qty (int) and region (string). What does df.fillna(0) do?",
 o:["Fills NULLs in all columns with 0 / '0'","Fills NULLs only in numeric columns such as qty","Fails because region is a string","Drops rows with NULL"],
 a:1, e:"fillna(0) só preenche colunas numéricas. Para várias: fillna({'qty': 0, 'region': 'n/a'})."},
{m:2,s:3,q:"With ANSI mode enabled, CAST('abc' AS INT) fails the query. Which expression returns NULL instead?",
 o:["cast_safe('abc', INT)","try_cast('abc' AS INT)","CAST('abc' AS INT) IGNORE ERRORS","nullif('abc', INT)"],
 a:1, e:"try_cast devolve NULL em vez de falhar."},
{m:2,s:3,code:"split(col('full_name'), ' ')",
 q:"How do you get the FIRST element of the resulting array?",
 o:["getItem(1)","getItem(0) or element_at(..., 1)","element_at(..., 0)","first()"],
 a:1, e:"Indexação com [i]/getItem começa em 0; element_at começa em 1."},
{m:2,s:3,q:"A pipeline with a streaming table built with AUTO CDC ... STORED AS SCD TYPE 2 is fully refreshed. What happens to the history?",
 o:["It is preserved","It is lost; the table is rebuilt from the available source data","It is moved to an archive table","Only the last version is lost"],
 a:1, e:"Um full refresh apaga o histórico SCD2: a tabela é reconstruída a partir do que existir na fonte."},
{m:2,s:3,q:"You need to replace a table's data AND change its schema, while keeping table history and grants. Which command?",
 o:["DROP TABLE then CREATE TABLE","INSERT OVERWRITE","CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE ... AS SELECT","DELETE FROM then INSERT"],
 a:2, e:"CREATE OR REPLACE mantém histórico e grants. INSERT OVERWRITE falha se o schema mudar; DROP perde histórico e grants."},
{m:2,s:3,q:"What is the default behavior of an expectation defined WITHOUT an ON VIOLATION clause?",
 o:["Drop the row","Fail the update","Keep the row and record the violation (warn)","Quarantine the row"],
 a:2, e:"Sem ON VIOLATION a linha mantém-se e a violação fica nas métricas."},
{m:2,s:3,q:"A Gold aggregate is expensive to compute and must be refreshed when sources change, and queried by BI. Which object?",
 o:["View","Materialized view","Temporary view","Streaming table"],
 a:1, e:"Materialized view guarda o resultado e é atualizada (REFRESH, agendada ou incremental). Uma view recalcula sempre."},
{m:2,s:3,q:"A source is append-only and every row must be processed exactly once incrementally. Which object fits best?",
 o:["Materialized view","Streaming table","View","External table"],
 a:1, e:"Streaming table = append incremental, cada linha processada uma vez."},
{m:2,s:3,q:"In Python declarative pipelines, which decorator drops rows that violate a rule?",
 o:["@dp.expect","@dp.expect_or_drop","@dp.expect_or_fail","@dp.validate"],
 a:1, e:"@dp.expect (warn), @dp.expect_or_drop (drop), @dp.expect_or_fail (fail). Import: from pyspark import pipelines as dp."},
// S4
{m:2,s:4,q:"A task should send an alert only if any upstream task failed. Which 'Run if' condition?",
 o:["ALL_SUCCESS","ALL_DONE","AT_LEAST_ONE_FAILED","NONE_FAILED"],
 a:2, e:"AT_LEAST_ONE_FAILED serve para alertas e tratamento de falhas."},
{m:2,s:4,q:"Three tasks use the same configuration and should share one classic cluster within a job run. What do you configure?",
 o:["An all-purpose cluster","A shared job cluster referenced by job_cluster_key","Three separate job clusters","A SQL warehouse"],
 a:1, e:"job_cluster_key permite que várias tasks partilhem o mesmo job cluster."},
{m:2,s:4,q:"A job must process a list of 50 country codes, running the same notebook once per country. Which task type?",
 o:["If/else condition","For each","Run Job","Pipeline"],
 a:1, e:"For each itera sobre uma lista e corre uma task aninhada por elemento."},
{m:2,s:4,q:"A job should run only when the source table silver.orders is updated. Which trigger?",
 o:["Scheduled","File arrival","Table update","Continuous"],
 a:2, e:"Table update trigger dispara quando uma ou mais tabelas (any/all) são atualizadas."},
{m:2,s:4,q:"A task must be killed if it runs longer than 1 hour. Which setting?",
 o:["A duration warning threshold","timeout_seconds = 3600","max_retries = 1","max_concurrent_runs = 1"],
 a:1, e:"timeout_seconds mata a tentativa (estado Timed Out). Um warning só notifica."},
{m:2,s:4,q:"How can Task B reference a value set by Task 'ingest' with key 'row_count' in its parameters?",
 o:["{{tasks.ingest.values.row_count}}","${ingest.row_count}","{{job.ingest.row_count}}","$row_count"],
 a:0, e:"Referência dinâmica a task values: {{tasks.<task>.values.<key>}}."},
{m:2,s:4,q:"A branch of a job must run only if a parameter 'full_load' equals 'true'. Which task type implements this?",
 o:["For each","If/else condition","Run Job","SQL alert"],
 a:1, e:"If/else condition avalia uma condição e escolhe o ramo a seguir."},
// S5
{m:2,s:5,q:"Where must the main bundle configuration file be located?",
 o:["One databricks.yml at the root of the bundle project","One databricks.yml in every folder","Inside the resources/ folder only","Anywhere, as long as it is named bundle.json"],
 a:0, e:"Há um único databricks.yml na raiz; recursos podem estar noutros ficheiros incluídos (ex.: resources/*.yml)."},
{m:2,s:5,q:"A variable is set in targets.prod.variables, via BUNDLE_VAR_catalog, and via --var on the CLI. Which wins?",
 o:["The target value","The BUNDLE_VAR_ environment variable","The --var CLI flag","The default"],
 a:2, e:"Precedência: --var > BUNDLE_VAR_x > variable-overrides.json > variáveis do target > default."},
{m:2,s:5,q:"When are bundle variables resolved?",
 o:["At deploy time","Each time the job runs","Only during bundle init","When the notebook is opened"],
 a:0, e:"As variáveis resolvem-se no deploy. Para valores por execução, usa job parameters."},
{m:2,s:5,q:"A job was created manually in the UI and must now be managed by a bundle. Which command helps?",
 o:["databricks bundle init --from-job","databricks bundle generate job --existing-job-id <id> (with --bind)","databricks jobs export","databricks bundle deploy --import"],
 a:1, e:"bundle generate job cria a configuração a partir de um job existente; --bind liga o recurso ao job."},
{m:2,s:5,q:"A target uses mode: development. Which behavior applies?",
 o:["Resources are prefixed with [dev <user>] and schedules/triggers are paused","Resources are deployed as the service principal","Deployment requires approval","All variables are ignored"],
 a:0, e:"mode: development acrescenta o prefixo [dev utilizador] e pausa schedules e triggers, para não interferir com produção."},
// S6
{m:2,s:6,q:"The Spark UI shows a large amount of 'spill to disk' in a stage. What is the likely cause?",
 o:["Partitions too large for executor memory","Too few Delta versions","The table is managed","Photon is enabled"],
 a:0, e:"Spill = partições grandes demais para a memória. Solução: partições mais pequenas ou nós com mais memória."},
{m:2,s:6,q:"A query runs on serverless compute and you need to investigate skew. Where do you look?",
 o:["Spark UI","Query profile","Ganglia","Driver logs only"],
 a:1, e:"Em serverless não há Spark UI: usa o query profile (indica DATA_SKEW, DATA_SPILL…)."},
{m:2,s:6,q:"A job run shows task D as 'Upstream failed'. How should you troubleshoot?",
 o:["Fix task D's code","Go up the DAG to the first failed task and inspect it","Increase D's retries","Change D's cluster"],
 a:1, e:"Upstream failed significa que uma task anterior falhou; sobe no grafo até à primeira falha."},
{m:2,s:6,q:"After VACUUM with the default retention, a query using VERSION AS OF 3 (from 30 days ago) fails. Why?",
 o:["Time travel is disabled by OPTIMIZE","VACUUM deleted the data files needed by that old version","VERSION AS OF only works on managed tables","DESCRIBE HISTORY must be run first"],
 a:1, e:"VACUUM (retenção por defeito 7 dias) apaga ficheiros não referenciados e corta o time travel para versões antigas."},
// S7
{m:2,s:7,q:"A group should be able to see table names and metadata in Catalog Explorer, but NOT read data. Which privilege?",
 o:["SELECT","BROWSE","MODIFY","USE CONNECTION"],
 a:1, e:"BROWSE permite ver metadados sem ler dados."},
{m:2,s:7,q:"A central security team wants one rule that masks every column tagged pii=email in all current and future tables of a catalog. What should they use?",
 o:["A column mask on each table","ABAC policy with governed tags","A dynamic view per table","REVOKE SELECT on the catalog"],
 a:1, e:"ABAC: governed tags + CREATE POLICY ... ON CATALOG ... MATCH COLUMNS has_tag_value(...). Cobre tabelas atuais e futuras."},
{m:2,s:7,q:"A MANAGED table was dropped by mistake 2 days ago. What can recover it?",
 o:["RESTORE TABLE","UNDROP TABLE","VACUUM","It cannot be recovered"],
 a:1, e:"UNDROP recupera tabelas managed apagadas nos últimos 7 dias."},
{m:2,s:7,q:"Where can you query who accessed which tables in Unity Catalog?",
 o:["system.access.audit","system.billing.usage","DESCRIBE HISTORY","information_schema.tables only"],
 a:0, e:"Os logs de auditoria estão na system table system.access.audit."},
{m:2,s:7,q:"A privilege is granted on a schema. Which objects does it apply to?",
 o:["Only tables that existed at grant time","All current and future objects in the schema","Only views","Only the schema itself"],
 a:1, e:"A herança desce do catalog/schema para tudo o que existe e vier a existir."},
{m:2,s:7,q:"Which principals should privileges be granted to in Unity Catalog?",
 o:["Workspace-local groups","Account-level groups and service principals","Only individual users","The metastore admin only"],
 a:1, e:"Concede a account groups e service principals (pelo application ID), nunca a grupos locais do workspace."},
{m:2,s:7,q:"A group must apply a masking function defined in Unity Catalog. Which privilege on the function?",
 o:["SELECT","EXECUTE","MODIFY","USE SCHEMA only"],
 a:1, e:"Para usar uma função (ou máscara) é preciso EXECUTE."},
// ───────────────────────── MOCK 3 (cenários inspirados no Notion, escritos de novo) ─────────────────────────
// S1
{m:3,s:1,q:"A development workspace and an analytics workspace in the same region both need the governed 'sales' catalog with the same permissions. What is the recommended approach?",
 o:["Deep clone the tables into each workspace","Attach both workspaces to the region's single Unity Catalog metastore","Create a second metastore for the analytics workspace","Share the catalog with OpenSharing between the two workspaces"],
 a:1, e:"Um metastore por região, ligado a vários workspaces: o catálogo aparece em ambos e os grants valem nos dois. Copiar tabelas cria duas versões da verdade."},
{m:3,s:1,q:"A Structured Streaming notebook that worked on classic compute fails on serverless with INFINITE_STREAMING_TRIGGER_NOT_SUPPORTED. The code sets no trigger. What is the fix?",
 o:["Set trigger(processingTime='1 minute')","Set trigger(availableNow=True)","Increase the number of workers","Enable Photon"],
 a:1, e:"Sem trigger, o defeito é processingTime 0 (corre para sempre), que o serverless rejeita. Serverless só aceita AvailableNow (e Once, deprecated). Para fluxo contínuo usa um job contínuo ou uma pipeline em modo contínuo."},
{m:3,s:1,q:"A job task runs a notebook that contains Python cells, and the task is configured to use a SQL warehouse. What happens?",
 o:["The Python cells are skipped","The task fails, because SQL warehouses only run SQL","The warehouse converts Python to SQL","It runs, but without Photon"],
 a:1, e:"Um notebook só pode correr num SQL warehouse se for todo SQL. Para Python usa serverless jobs ou job compute."},
// S2
{m:3,s:2,q:"A supplier re-uploads a corrected file with the same name. COPY INTO already loaded the original version. What is the correct way to fix the table?",
 o:["Run COPY INTO again; it detects the modified file","Delete the rows from the original file, then COPY INTO with FILES = ('file.csv') and COPY_OPTIONS ('force' = 'true')","Run COPY INTO with 'force' = 'true' on the whole folder","Run VACUUM, then COPY INTO"],
 a:1, e:"COPY INTO ignora ficheiros já carregados mesmo se modificados. force recarrega, mas não substitui as linhas antigas: apaga-as primeiro e usa FILES para limitar o reload a esse ficheiro."},
{m:3,s:2,q:"In COPY INTO, which option lets the TARGET table's schema evolve when the source files gain new columns?",
 o:["FORMAT_OPTIONS ('mergeSchema' = 'true')","COPY_OPTIONS ('mergeSchema' = 'true')","FORMAT_OPTIONS ('inferSchema' = 'true')","COPY_OPTIONS ('force' = 'true')"],
 a:1, e:"FORMAT_OPTIONS (inferSchema, mergeSchema) moldam o schema lido da fonte; COPY_OPTIONS mergeSchema evolui a tabela de destino."},
{m:3,s:2,q:"An engineer reads a table over JDBC with partitionColumn='order_id', lowerBound=1, upperBound=1000, numPartitions=8, expecting only the first 1,000 orders, but gets millions of rows. Why?",
 o:["numPartitions is too high","lowerBound and upperBound only define the partition stride; they don't filter rows","JDBC ignores partitionColumn on serverless","The driver needs fetchSize"],
 a:1, e:"Os bounds só definem como as partições são divididas; todas as linhas são lidas. Para filtrar, põe um WHERE na subquery do dbtable."},
{m:3,s:2,q:"An admin wants analysts to build ServiceNow ingestion pipelines without ever seeing the ServiceNow credentials. What should the admin do?",
 o:["Share the password in a secret scope readable by analysts","Create a Unity Catalog connection and grant USE CONNECTION (plus USE CATALOG, USE SCHEMA and CREATE TABLE on the target)","Grant CREATE CONNECTION on the metastore to the analysts","Give the analysts workspace admin rights"],
 a:1, e:"A connection guarda as credenciais; USE CONNECTION deixa construir pipelines sem as ver. CREATE CONNECTION não é necessário para usar uma connection existente."},
{m:3,s:2,q:"An Auto Loader stream in directory listing mode reads a path that now holds millions of files, and each run gets slower. What is the recommended change?",
 o:["Switch to COPY INTO","Enable file events on the external location and use file notification mode (cloudFiles.useManagedFileEvents), keeping the same checkpoint","Delete the checkpoint and restart","Lower maxFilesPerTrigger to 1"],
 a:1, e:"File notification com file events é o modo recomendado para grandes volumes; mudar de modo mantém o processamento exactly-once com o mesmo checkpoint."},
{m:3,s:2,q:"The same JSON files are loaded once with read_files and once with Auto Loader, both with default options. What difference do you expect in the column types?",
 o:["None, both infer types","read_files infers types; Auto Loader infers JSON columns as STRING unless cloudFiles.inferColumnTypes is true","Auto Loader infers types; read_files returns strings","Both return a single VARIANT column"],
 a:1, e:"Defeitos diferentes: Auto Loader infere JSON/CSV/XML como string (evita conflitos de tipos); read_files infere tipos."},
{m:3,s:2,q:"A table moves a JSON column from STRING to VARIANT, and the expression raw:items[*].sku stops working. What should be used on the VARIANT column?",
 o:["raw.items.sku","LATERAL variant_explode(raw:items) and then value:sku","explode(raw:items[*])","from_json(raw:items)"],
 a:1, e:"O wildcard [*] só funciona em colunas JSON string. Em VARIANT usa variant_explode. E atenção: em VARIANT os nomes dos campos são case sensitive."},
{m:3,s:2,q:"An analyst wants a table from a single 3 GB CSV on their laptop. The 'Create or modify table' upload page rejects it. What works?",
 o:["Zip the file and upload it again","Upload the file to a Unity Catalog volume and create the table from there (read_files, COPY INTO or Catalog Explorer)","Split it into 20 files and use the upload page","Use Lakeflow Connect"],
 a:1, e:"A página de upload aceita até 10 ficheiros com menos de 2 GB no total, sem comprimidos. Um volume aceita ficheiros maiores e guarda o ficheiro para recargas."},
{m:3,s:2,q:"A security team ingests delivered audit log files with Auto Loader (default options) and finds events in system.access.audit that never reach their bronze table. Why, and what fixes it?",
 o:["Audit logs are Parquet; set cloudFiles.format to parquet","Delivered files can be rewritten with extra lines and Auto Loader processes each path once; set cloudFiles.allowOverwrites = true and deduplicate","Switch to file notification mode","Start a new checkpoint every day"],
 a:1, e:"Os ficheiros de audit log entregues podem ser reescritos. Com allowOverwrites o ficheiro é reprocessado; depois deduplica (ex.: MERGE só com INSERT). A alternativa mais simples é ler system.access.audit."},
// S3
{m:3,s:3,q:"On a recent runtime with ANSI mode enabled, CAST(amount AS DECIMAL(10,2)) fails because some bronze rows contain 'N/A'. What is the recommended fix?",
 o:["Set spark.sql.ansi.enabled = false for the session","Use try_cast(amount AS DECIMAL(10,2)) and handle the resulting NULLs","fillna('0') before the cast","Use CAST(... AS STRING)"],
 a:1, e:"try_cast devolve NULL para valores inválidos. Desligar ANSI afeta a sessão toda (ex.: overflow silencioso). fillna não ajuda porque 'N/A' não é NULL."},
{m:3,s:3,q:"order_date strings look like 07/03/2026 meaning 7 March. Which expression parses them correctly?",
 o:["to_date(order_date)","to_date(order_date, 'dd/mm/yyyy')","to_date(order_date, 'dd/MM/yyyy')","CAST(order_date AS DATE)"],
 a:2, e:"Sem formato, to_date comporta-se como cast (espera yyyy-MM-dd). M é mês, m é minuto."},
{m:3,s:3,q:"A daily MERGE into silver fails with DELTA_MULTIPLE_SOURCE_ROW_MATCHING_TARGET_ROW_IN_MERGE. What is the cause and fix?",
 o:["The target has duplicates; run OPTIMIZE","The source batch has several rows for the same key; keep only the latest row per key before merging","The merge condition is missing; add ON","Schema evolution is disabled; add mergeSchema"],
 a:1, e:"A fonte tem duas versões da mesma chave. Deduplica (row_number por chave, ordenado por timestamp desc) antes do MERGE."},
{m:3,s:3,code:"orders.join(prices,\n  (orders.product_id == prices.product_id) & (orders.region == prices.region))\n  .select('product_id', 'unit_price')",
 q:"The select fails with AMBIGUOUS_REFERENCE. What is the simplest fix?",
 o:["Drop 'product_id' after the join","Join on a list of column names: orders.join(prices, ['product_id', 'region'])","Use a cross join","Use unionByName"],
 a:1, e:"Join por lista de nomes (ou USING) deixa uma só cópia de cada chave. Dropar pelo nome depois do join por expressão remove as duas cópias."},
{m:3,s:3,q:"ALTER TABLE t RENAME COLUMN cust_name TO customer_name fails on a Delta table. What is required?",
 o:["OPTIMIZE the table first","Enable column mapping: ALTER TABLE t SET TBLPROPERTIES ('delta.columnMapping.mode' = 'name')","Convert the table to external","Use withColumnRenamed and overwrite the table"],
 a:1, e:"RENAME e DROP COLUMN precisam de column mapping e só mudam metadados. Atenção: podem interromper leituras em streaming da tabela."},
{m:3,s:3,q:"With ANSI mode on, split(order_ref, '-')[2] fails with INVALID_ARRAY_INDEX for short values like 'GB-LON'. Which expression returns NULL instead?",
 o:["split(order_ref, '-')[3]","element_at(split(order_ref, '-'), 2)","try_element_at(split(order_ref, '-'), 3)","getItem(2)"],
 a:2, e:"try_element_at devolve NULL fora do limite e conta a partir de 1 (o 3.º elemento é o índice 3)."},
{m:3,s:3,q:"A materialized view's scheduled refreshes start failing after its owner moved teams and lost access to the source schema. Analysts can still query it. What is the fix?",
 o:["Grant the analysts SELECT on the source tables","Change the MV owner to an identity that keeps SELECT on the sources, such as a service principal","Convert the MV to a view","Run REFRESH as an analyst"],
 a:1, e:"O refresh corre com as permissões do dono. Os resultados antigos continuam legíveis, mas ficam desatualizados."},
{m:3,s:3,q:"A gold table is written by a nightly job, a backfill notebook and manual SQL fixes. It must never contain a negative amount. What enforces this for every writer?",
 o:["An expectation with ON VIOLATION FAIL UPDATE","A Delta CHECK constraint on the table","A WHERE filter in the nightly job","A row filter"],
 a:1, e:"CHECK (e NOT NULL) da Delta rejeitam qualquer transação que viole a regra, seja quem for a escrever. Expectations só se aplicam dentro da pipeline que as define."},
{m:3,s:3,q:"Auditors need every rejected record and the reason it was rejected. Which approach fits?",
 o:["ON VIOLATION DROP ROW","Quarantine: write valid rows to silver and the rest to a quarantine table","ON VIOLATION FAIL UPDATE","A warn expectation"],
 a:1, e:"DROP só guarda a contagem, não as linhas. A quarentena guarda os registos rejeitados; garante que cada linha (incluindo com NULLs) vai para exatamente uma tabela."},
{m:3,s:3,q:"The average order value looks too high. Some orders have NULL amount, and the business rule says a missing amount means 0. What should you compute?",
 o:["avg(amount)","avg(coalesce(amount, 0))","sum(amount) / count(amount)","count(*)"],
 a:1, e:"avg ignora NULLs, por isso calcula a média só das linhas com valor. Se NULL significa 0, usa coalesce."},
// S4
{m:3,s:4,q:"An ingest task sometimes finds no new files, and the transform should not run in that case. What is the best design?",
 o:["Make ingest fail when there are no files","Set a task value with the row count and add an If/else condition task ({{tasks.ingest.values.rows}} > 0) before the transform","Use Run if = ALL_DONE on the transform","Use a Continuous trigger"],
 a:1, e:"Run if reage a sucesso/falha, não a dados. Falhar de propósito marcaria um run saudável como falhado."},
{m:3,s:4,q:"An If/else condition {{tasks.count.values.n}} == 0 never matches, although the count is zero. The value arrives as 0.0. Why?",
 o:["Task values can't be numbers","== and != compare values as strings; use a numeric operator such as <= 0","If/else only works with job parameters","The condition needs ALL_DONE"],
 a:1, e:"Em If/else, == e != comparam strings; <, >, <=, >= comparam números."},
{m:3,s:4,q:"Which Quartz cron expression schedules a job daily at 06:30?",
 o:["30 6 * * *","0 30 6 * * ?","6 30 * * * ?","0 6 30 * * ?"],
 a:1, e:"Quartz tem 6 campos e começa nos segundos: segundos minutos horas dia-do-mês mês dia-da-semana. Define também o timezone (ex.: Europe/Lisbon)."},
{m:3,s:4,q:"A job uses a table update trigger on silver.orders but never starts, even though the table is updated. What is the most likely cause?",
 o:["Table update triggers only work on views","The job's Run as principal lacks SELECT on the monitored table","The table is managed","The trigger needs a file arrival path"],
 a:1, e:"O trigger avalia com a identidade Run as; sem SELECT não consegue avaliar e o job nunca corre. Configura notificações de falha para dares por isso."},
{m:3,s:4,q:"Which statement about Continuous jobs is correct?",
 o:["They support task dependencies and per-task retry policies","They keep one run active, can't use task dependencies or retry policies, and restart with exponential backoff after failures","They run on a Quartz schedule every minute","They require a file arrival location"],
 a:1, e:"Um job contínuo mantém sempre um run ativo; não usa dependências entre tasks nem retry policies; reinicia com exponential backoff."},
{m:3,s:4,q:"A source system overwrites the same file name in a volume every day, and a file arrival trigger on that path never fires. Why?",
 o:["File arrival triggers only watch external locations","File arrival triggers fire only for new files, not overwrites","The trigger needs Wait after last change = 0","The volume must be managed"],
 a:1, e:"Só ficheiros novos disparam o trigger. Pede nomes únicos ou usa outro trigger."},
{m:3,s:4,q:"A job contains a pipeline task and has max_concurrent_runs = 5. How many runs of this job can be active at once?",
 o:["5","1","Unlimited","0"],
 a:1, e:"Um job com pipeline task fica limitado a 1 run concorrente, porque uma pipeline só corre uma update de cada vez."},
// S5
{m:3,s:5,q:"An engineer runs databricks bundle run orders_job -t test --var='catalog=other' but the job still writes to test_catalog. Why, and what should be done?",
 o:["--var is only valid on validate","Bundle variables are resolved at deploy time; expose the value as a job parameter and pass it with --params, or redeploy","The variable needs a default","The test target is in production mode"],
 a:1, e:"As variáveis fixam-se no deploy. Para valores por run, usa job parameters (--params catalog=other)."},
{m:3,s:5,q:"A developer runs databricks bundle deploy -t prod from a feature branch. The prod target has mode: production and git.branch: main, and validation fails. What is the right response?",
 o:["Add --force","Merge the change to main and let CI deploy from main as the production service principal","Switch the target to development mode","Delete git.branch from the target"],
 a:1, e:"O production mode verifica se o branch atual é o do target. --force contorna a verificação, mas ela existe precisamente para impedir isso."},
{m:3,s:5,q:"A team generates YAML for a UI-created job and deploys it without binding. What happens?",
 o:["The existing job is updated","A second, duplicate job is created","The deploy fails","The UI job is deleted"],
 a:1, e:"Para adotar o job existente: databricks bundle generate job --existing-job-id <id> --bind (ou bundle deployment bind)."},
{m:3,s:5,q:"A CI step runs databricks bundle destroy -t test and never finishes. What is missing?",
 o:["--force-lock","--auto-approve","-o json","--select"],
 a:1, e:"destroy pede confirmação; em automação usa --auto-approve. --force-lock serve só para um lock deixado por um deploy interrompido."},
{m:3,s:5,q:"A user has CAN EDIT on a colleague's Git folder. Editing works, but switching branches, Pull and Commit & Push fail. Why?",
 o:["The Git credential expired","Those operations require CAN MANAGE on the Git folder","Git folders don't support branches","The repo must be public"],
 a:1, e:"Branch, pull e push precisam de CAN MANAGE. A boa prática é cada pessoa ter a sua Git folder (o branch pertence à pasta)."},
// S6
{m:3,s:6,q:"A job got 10 minutes slower with no code or data change. The run's Duration breakdown shows the extra time in 'Waiting for resources'. Which change helps?",
 o:["Tune spark.sql.shuffle.partitions","Reduce compute acquisition time: instance pools, serverless (performance optimized) or grouping jobs into one multi-task job","Add a broadcast hint","Run OPTIMIZE on the tables"],
 a:1, e:"Se o Running não mudou, o problema é obter compute, não o código."},
{m:3,s:6,q:"An aggregation per device_id is dominated by one test device; AQE is on but the stage is still skewed. Why, and what helps?",
 o:["AQE handles skew only in joins (sort merge / shuffle hash), not aggregations; salt the key and aggregate in two stages","AQE needs more workers","Lower spark.sql.shuffle.partitions","Broadcast the table"],
 a:0, e:"O skew join do AQE não se aplica a agregações. Baixar shuffle.partitions aumenta cada partição, incluindo a enviesada."},
{m:3,s:6,q:"An engineer ran ALTER TABLE t CLUSTER BY (region, order_date) yesterday, but queries filtering on region still scan most files. What should they run?",
 o:["VACUUM t","OPTIMIZE t FULL","ANALYZE TABLE t","Recreate the table"],
 a:1, e:"Mudar as chaves não reescreve os dados existentes. OPTIMIZE FULL re-clusteriza tudo (pode demorar horas numa tabela grande)."},
{m:3,s:6,q:"Predictive optimization is enabled on the catalog, but one table never gets OPTIMIZE or VACUUM. What is the likely reason?",
 o:["The table has liquid clustering","The table is an external table; predictive optimization runs only on Unity Catalog managed tables","Predictive optimization runs only on Mondays","The table has fewer than 1,000 files"],
 a:1, e:"Para tabelas external: converter para managed (SET MANAGED) ou agendar OPTIMIZE e VACUUM à mão."},
// S7
{m:3,s:7,q:"A schema owner grants SELECT on finance.reporting.invoices to auditors, but they still get a permission error. What is missing?",
 o:["ALL PRIVILEGES on the table","USE CATALOG on finance and USE SCHEMA on finance.reporting","MODIFY on the table","BROWSE on the metastore"],
 a:1, e:"Qualquer operação precisa de USE CATALOG e USE SCHEMA nos pais. Só o dono (ou quem tem MANAGE) do catálogo/schema pode concedê-los."},
{m:3,s:7,q:"Sales staff are in account groups sales_UK, sales_FR, etc. Each team should see only its country's rows. Which row filter function body fits?",
 o:["RETURN is_member('sales_' || country)","RETURN is_account_group_member('sales_' || country)","RETURN current_user() = country","RETURN country IN (SELECT * FROM groups)"],
 a:1, e:"is_account_group_member testa grupos de conta (os do Unity Catalog); is_member é para grupos locais do workspace. Uma só tabela serve todas as equipas."},
{m:3,s:7,q:"A job on dedicated access mode with Databricks Runtime 15.3 can't read a table that has a column mask. What fixes it?",
 o:["Remove the mask","Use Databricks Runtime 15.4 LTS or above (with serverless enabled in the workspace), or standard access mode / a SQL warehouse","Grant MODIFY","Add the user to the mask's EXCEPT list"],
 a:1, e:"Ler tabelas com filtros/máscaras em dedicated exige 15.4 LTS+ e serverless ativo, porque a filtragem corre em serverless."},
{m:3,s:7,q:"Every email column in the 'crm' catalog (300 tables, growing weekly) must be masked, and table owners must not be able to remove the masking. What is the best approach?",
 o:["A column mask on each table","Tag the email columns and create one ABAC column mask policy ON CATALOG crm with MATCH COLUMNS has_tag_value('pii', 'email')","A dynamic view per table","REVOKE SELECT from everyone"],
 a:1, e:"A policy ABAC cobre tabelas atuais e futuras (quando as colunas são marcadas) e os donos das tabelas não a podem sobrepor."},
{m:3,s:7,q:"A table is tagged pii, but its columns are not tagged. An ABAC column mask policy uses MATCH COLUMNS has_tag_value('pii', ...). Are the columns masked?",
 o:["Yes, columns inherit table tags","No, MATCH COLUMNS only checks tags set directly on columns","Yes, but only for new rows","Only on SQL warehouses"],
 a:1, e:"As tags de coluna não herdam da tabela, schema ou catálogo."},
{m:3,s:7,q:"You need to move an external Delta table to managed storage while keeping its name, permissions and history. Which command?",
 o:["CREATE TABLE new AS SELECT * FROM old","ALTER TABLE t SET MANAGED","ALTER TABLE t SET EXTERNAL","CONVERT TO DELTA"],
 a:1, e:"SET MANAGED converte no lugar (UNSET MANAGED reverte até 14 dias). Um CTAS cria outra tabela, sem permissões nem histórico."},
{m:3,s:7,q:"An admin drops a SQL UDF that a table still uses as a column mask. What happens?",
 o:["The mask is removed automatically","The table becomes inaccessible until the mask is dropped (ALTER COLUMN ... DROP MASK)","The column shows NULL to everyone","Nothing"],
 a:1, e:"Primeiro faz DROP MASK / DROP ROW FILTER, só depois apaga a função."},
];
